From: OpenATV
Subject: [PATCH] opkg: protect flash when installing legacy picon packages

Count the real IPK payload before changing files or running package scripts.
Limit internal flash to 1000 files and 10 MiB with space/inode reserves;
allow larger packages only on an actual HDD or USB-backed filesystem.
Do not apply runtime storage policy while constructing an offline rootfs.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenATV receiver storage policy]

diff --git a/libopkg/CMakeLists.txt b/libopkg/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/libopkg/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libopkg/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -104,6 +104,7 @@
     opkg_utils.c
     opkg_verify.c
     parse_util.c
+    picon_storage.c
     pkg.c
     pkg_depends.c
     pkg_dest.c
